Controller layout from the launcher, button by button (TOBIICHI_MANDO).
- ps2_pad.cpp: TOBIICHI_MANDO="action=button,button;..." with the action names of TOBIICHI_TECLAS (buttons only: up ..
  furia, so magics, Blade of Artemis and Rage of the Gods can sit on any button too) and raylib gamepad buttons
  (GAMEPAD_BUTTON_*: 1-4 d-pad, 5-8 face, 9-12 LB LT RB RT, 13 back, 15 start, 16/17 stick clicks). With it, every pad
  button (d-pad, start, select and stick clicks included) follows the map instead of the fixed modern / classic layout
  (TOBIICHI_DMC5_CONTROLS); the sticks stay analog. Without it nothing changes.
The launcher's Controls tab writes the variable (Controller section, buttons captured from the controller through XInput).

